{"entryId":"1348","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1348:1","sourceSha256":"8c93a13bcccbe9112a1bb222e1956b8a2209466cc00089991e485500fb9530f5","englishSha256":"b0d33c986a0262f4c229b66561ee608a838215867aae63614e81adbe23200c83","citations":[{"id":"1348:1:citation-01","he":[120,166],"en":[267,280],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_46b.10"},"reference":"Sanhedrin 46b:10","assessment":"The checked Bavli names Rav Chama and has Rav Acha bar Yaakov speak without to him. Preserve the reported witnesses and grammatical argument.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sanhedrin 46b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_46b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1348:1:citation-02","he":[337,369],"en":[606,616],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Taanit_16b.2"},"reference":"Taanit 16b:2","assessment":"Taanit gives this chain as an alternate attribution.","evidence":[{"reference":"Taanit 16b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Taanit_16b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1348:1:citation-03","he":[371,394],"en":[618,650],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_86a.6"},"reference":"Ketubot 86a:6","assessment":"Ketubot gives the exact Amemar attribution. The transmitted Chama is bare and this does not establish an identity with the Sanhedrin figure.","evidence":[{"reference":"Ketubot 86a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_86a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2],"holds":[{"raw":"והגירסא שלפנינו רב אחא ובעין יעקב הגירסא רב חסדא","reason":"The checked Bavli has Rav Chama. The precise reported Ein Yaakov readings remain uncollated. Preserve the grammar argument and identity qualification.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sanhedrin 46b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_46b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"אמר אמימר משמיה דרב חמא","reason":"The exact Ketubot statement names a bare Rav Chama, whose identity remains open.","evidence":[{"reference":"Ketubot 86a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_86a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"The retrieved Bavli gives Chama and the third-person formulation. The independent Amemar attribution is exact, with bare Chama.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Sanhedrin 46b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_46b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Taanit 16b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Taanit_16b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Ketubot 86a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_86a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
